WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.350 --> 00:00:02.540
Have you ever had an imaginary friend?

00:00:02.540 --> 00:00:06.560
Maybe you did when you were very little and
then forgot all about it.

00:00:06.560 --> 00:00:12.590
That first friend you ever had, the one you
told all your secrets, your fears, the one

00:00:12.590 --> 00:00:17.150
you trusted and listened to for advice when
you weren’t sure if something was right

00:00:17.150 --> 00:00:18.260
or wrong.

00:00:18.260 --> 00:00:23.530
The one you swore you would carry with you
everywhere you went, that sacred pact that

00:00:23.530 --> 00:00:26.270
slowly drifted into nothingness.

00:00:26.270 --> 00:00:28.040
And then you forgot.

00:00:28.040 --> 00:00:32.330
Well, what if those imaginary friends weren’t
imaginary after all.

00:00:32.330 --> 00:00:33.500
Just what were they?

00:00:33.500 --> 00:00:35.059
Where did they come from?

00:00:35.059 --> 00:00:40.280
And are they still out there somewhere, waiting
for us to think them back into existence?

00:00:40.280 --> 00:00:45.909
Today’s story begins not in our childhood,
but deep inside a hidden underground facility

00:00:45.909 --> 00:00:52.449
where a man sits in his enclosed habitat protected
by round-the-clock armed SCP Foundation security

00:00:52.449 --> 00:00:53.519
personnel.

00:00:53.519 --> 00:00:59.030
This man is a middle-aged normal human being
without any unique physical characteristics.

00:00:59.030 --> 00:01:04.309
He is not a member of the O5 council, nor
is he a foreign dignitary or a person in any

00:01:04.309 --> 00:01:06.200
position of political power.

00:01:06.200 --> 00:01:11.500
And yet, the safety and protection of this
man’s life are of paramount importance.

00:01:11.500 --> 00:01:15.680
And what threatens that safety is the subject
of today’s video.

00:01:15.680 --> 00:01:24.130
The entity that hunts him, SCP-1447, also
known as The Tulpa.

00:01:24.130 --> 00:01:29.119
SCP-1447-1 is the Foundation’s designation
for the floating quasi-physical humanoid entity

00:01:29.119 --> 00:01:34.320
that resembles the appearance of a traditional
Buddhist monk, but whose face appears perpetually

00:01:34.320 --> 00:01:35.320
distorted.

00:01:35.320 --> 00:01:40.570
The word “Tulpa” is a Tibetan word that
means “emanation” or “magical creation”.

00:01:40.570 --> 00:01:45.409
The idea being that a practitioner of deep
meditation could focus hard enough to conjure

00:01:45.409 --> 00:01:50.659
a physical manifestation of a thought or an
idea.

00:01:50.659 --> 00:01:58.939
SCP-1447-1 is a Keter class entity currently
being held in an airtight 2.5x 2.5x 2.5 concrete

00:01:58.939 --> 00:02:02.439
container suspended above the ground in Bay
4.

00:02:02.439 --> 00:02:06.969
The cell is to be repeatedly reinforced with
steel plating, with regular inspections for

00:02:06.969 --> 00:02:09.640
any damage to the containment structure.

00:02:09.640 --> 00:02:16.000
Any cracks or breaks in SCP-1447-1’s containment
are to be reported immediately and considered

00:02:16.000 --> 00:02:17.840
a breach-level event.

00:02:17.840 --> 00:02:24.960
This is due to SCP-1447-1’s ability to insert
itself into breaches and cracks as small as

00:02:24.960 --> 00:02:27.290
200 micrometers in diameter.

00:02:27.290 --> 00:02:31.840
Meaning that even the smallest crack in its
containment enclosure will almost certainly

00:02:31.840 --> 00:02:34.960
lead to SCP-1447-1’s escape.

00:02:34.960 --> 00:02:40.140
While the tulpa seems uninterested in killing
anyone other than the facility’s previously

00:02:40.140 --> 00:02:44.890
mentioned resident, it will not hesitate in
killing any personnel that prevents it from

00:02:44.890 --> 00:02:47.720
achieving its principal goal.

00:02:47.720 --> 00:02:53.920
SCP-1447-1 appears unaffected by small arms
fire from standard-issue Foundation sidearms,

00:02:53.920 --> 00:02:56.780
seemingly impervious to any physical means
of damage.

00:02:56.780 --> 00:03:03.970
However, suppressive fire from high caliber
weaponry does seem to have an effect on SCP-1447-1,

00:03:03.970 --> 00:03:08.060
appearing to temporarily disrupt the projection
of its physical form.

00:03:08.060 --> 00:03:14.220
This concentration of high-caliber fire has
proven to be effective in forcing SCP-1447-1

00:03:14.220 --> 00:03:17.250
back into its containment enclosure.

00:03:17.250 --> 00:03:22.630
Explosives also seem to have the positive
effect of completely dissipating SCP-1447’s

00:03:22.630 --> 00:03:27.820
physical presence, however, this has the undesired
side effect of the entity then re-materializing

00:03:27.820 --> 00:03:30.760
somewhere else in the immediate vicinity.

00:03:30.760 --> 00:03:36.260
This rematerialization is not impeded by physical
structures, sometimes allowing the tulpa to

00:03:36.260 --> 00:03:40.100
bypass defensive positions and obstacles entirely.

00:03:40.100 --> 00:03:47.070
Although SCP-1447-1 appears on security footage
to hover slowly toward its intended target,

00:03:47.070 --> 00:03:51.250
SCP-1447’s behavior in containment is quite
the opposite.

00:03:51.250 --> 00:03:56.510
For 20 hours of the day, the tulpa moves around
its containment cell at a staggering 200km

00:03:56.510 --> 00:04:02.030
per hour, punching dents into its enclosure
hoping to create a weakness in the structure

00:04:02.030 --> 00:04:03.800
that it can exploit.

00:04:03.800 --> 00:04:07.650
It requires no rest and appears to have limitless
stamina.

00:04:07.650 --> 00:04:13.870
Despite researchers’ best efforts to film
SCP-1447-1 using a high-speed camera, its

00:04:13.870 --> 00:04:19.730
face is still impossible to see as it remains
in perpetual motion and only visible as a

00:04:19.730 --> 00:04:21.940
blur to the human eye.

00:04:21.940 --> 00:04:26.620
Attempts at communication with SCP-1447-1
have been inconclusive.

00:04:26.620 --> 00:04:31.220
When asked a question the tulpa will respond
with unintelligible garbled responses that,

00:04:31.220 --> 00:04:36.370
when slowed down, appear to be traditional
Tibetan mantras repeated hundreds of times

00:04:36.370 --> 00:04:38.190
a second.

00:04:38.190 --> 00:04:44.510
SCP-1447-1 does seem to exhibit signs of intelligence
and even deceit, as on one occasion it was

00:04:44.510 --> 00:04:50.000
observed goading security personnel into attacking
it with explosive devices as it was near the

00:04:50.000 --> 00:04:55.570
entrance of another SCP’s enclosure, leading
to a double breach event.

00:04:55.570 --> 00:05:01.100
SCP-1447-2 is the designation given to the
man currently confined to his quarters inside

00:05:01.100 --> 00:05:02.210
the containment site.

00:05:02.210 --> 00:05:07.000
He is a software and hardware engineer and
entrepreneur whose name has been redacted

00:05:07.000 --> 00:05:08.560
from official records.

00:05:08.560 --> 00:05:12.220
We will refer to him from here on simply as
“Steve”.

00:05:12.220 --> 00:05:17.030
The following is information the subject gave
SCP Foundation staff willingly.

00:05:17.030 --> 00:05:21.560
Steve was an accomplished man, excelling at
everything he did and finding a great level

00:05:21.560 --> 00:05:25.060
of success in the tech sector as a developer
and entrepreneur.

00:05:25.060 --> 00:05:29.810
And yet, with all the riches and fame that
his success brought him, he found himself

00:05:29.810 --> 00:05:31.030
wanting more.

00:05:31.030 --> 00:05:36.270
His obsessiveness for a sense of meaningful
fulfillment led him to drive away loved ones

00:05:36.270 --> 00:05:41.400
and dive further into his work, creating a
vicious cycle of self-isolation leaving him

00:05:41.400 --> 00:05:44.650
with a greater sense of unfulfillment from
his life.

00:05:44.650 --> 00:05:48.670
One day, Steve came to the realization that
what he needed was to split away from the

00:05:48.670 --> 00:05:50.680
reality he had created for himself.

00:05:50.680 --> 00:05:56.090
He needed to find peace, and he knew he couldn’t
do it where he currently was.

00:05:56.090 --> 00:06:00.840
He packed a bag and, without a second thought,
decided to leave everything behind without

00:06:00.840 --> 00:06:04.020
saying a word to anyone about where he was
going.

00:06:04.020 --> 00:06:07.640
But where was he going? he had thought to
himself.

00:06:07.640 --> 00:06:11.810
Following a trend of westerners traveling
to Asia to find a new sense of enlightenment,

00:06:11.810 --> 00:06:16.900
Steve boarded a plane to Qinghai Province,
China, where he joined an order of monastic

00:06:16.900 --> 00:06:17.900
monks.

00:06:17.900 --> 00:06:22.320
As he did with most aspects of his life, he
threw himself entirely into the practice,

00:06:22.320 --> 00:06:26.740
dressing like the brothers of the order in
the traditional monastic garb and even electing

00:06:26.740 --> 00:06:32.740
to shave his head bare, switching to a vegetarian
diet, and learning the Tibetan mantras.

00:06:32.740 --> 00:06:37.590
He put his sole effort into learning the art
of deep meditation, vowing to truly split

00:06:37.590 --> 00:06:42.630
away from the repetitive unfulfilling life
he had chosen to leave behind.

00:06:42.630 --> 00:06:47.060
During one particular lesson, Steve learned
from an elder brother at the monastery about

00:06:47.060 --> 00:06:52.199
the concept of a “tulpa”, a method where
a person enters deep focused meditation to

00:06:52.199 --> 00:06:57.280
conjure a physical visual manifestation of
a specific thought or emotion.

00:06:57.280 --> 00:07:01.480
Being new to the practice at the time, Steve
couldn’t find himself thinking of anything

00:07:01.480 --> 00:07:05.700
but the image of a laughing buddha he was
used to seeing every time he entered a local

00:07:05.700 --> 00:07:08.480
Chinese restaurant back in the United States.

00:07:08.480 --> 00:07:13.250
He remembered how the image made him feel
welcome, how the look of joy on the Buddha's

00:07:13.250 --> 00:07:16.080
face brought a look of joy to his own.

00:07:16.080 --> 00:07:20.240
Explaining this to the brothers at the monastery,
they promptly corrected him that this image

00:07:20.240 --> 00:07:25.980
is not an image of the buddha, as in the sense
of the buddha being a single defined deity,

00:07:25.980 --> 00:07:29.449
but just one of many interpretations of buddha.

00:07:29.449 --> 00:07:33.260
The laughing buddha is particularly a cultural
symbol of luck and abundance.

00:07:33.260 --> 00:07:38.760
The monks asked Steve to picture something
else when attempting to visualize a tulpa,

00:07:38.760 --> 00:07:41.460
such as an emotion that has taken form and
shape.

00:07:41.460 --> 00:07:46.320
But try as he could, Steve had become fixated
on the image of the popular laughing buddha,

00:07:46.320 --> 00:07:48.681
and could do little to imagine anything else.

00:07:48.681 --> 00:07:54.229
On his own, Steve meditated persistently in
this endeavor, truly expecting success and

00:07:54.229 --> 00:07:59.100
working towards it with the fervent drive
he put into every project in his life.

00:07:59.100 --> 00:08:04.740
And to the amazement of himself and the brothers
of the monastery, his tulpa slowly began to

00:08:04.740 --> 00:08:05.820
manifest.

00:08:05.820 --> 00:08:09.100
It was small at first, only an image that
he could see.

00:08:09.100 --> 00:08:13.550
He didn't think much of it, not thinking that
he had created anything real.

00:08:13.550 --> 00:08:17.680
He believed the image of the laughing buddha
in front of him was just an overactivation

00:08:17.680 --> 00:08:23.729
of the visual centers of his brain, most likely
due to the strain from long hours of meditation.

00:08:23.729 --> 00:08:28.240
Deciding to humor his imagination, he began
treating the tulpa like he would any brother

00:08:28.240 --> 00:08:32.999
of the temple, speaking to it out loud and
showing it respect and inclusion.

00:08:32.999 --> 00:08:36.269
It was like having his own imaginary friend.

00:08:36.269 --> 00:08:39.419
Yet over time, the tulpa began to become more
than just an image.

00:08:39.419 --> 00:08:44.939
It began to have a physical effect on objects
around him, a bucket kicked over, a chair

00:08:44.939 --> 00:08:47.000
pulled back as a brother went to sit down.

00:08:47.000 --> 00:08:53.341
The imaginary friend was now more like a mischievous
invisible prankster, but still, one that only

00:08:53.341 --> 00:08:54.490
he could see.

00:08:54.490 --> 00:08:58.879
The brothers began to grow weary of the tulpa,
and with it, grew weary of the foreigner that

00:08:58.879 --> 00:09:00.790
had brought it into existence.

00:09:00.790 --> 00:09:04.209
Meanwhile, Steve had become amazed at his
level of success.

00:09:04.209 --> 00:09:08.029
He began to wonder if he could manifest other
thoughts into existence.

00:09:08.029 --> 00:09:11.959
He began to think about his life, his career,
his level of success.

00:09:11.959 --> 00:09:16.420
He began to think about how he could apply
himself to impart his will on reality.

00:09:16.420 --> 00:09:18.329
How he wanted more.

00:09:18.329 --> 00:09:23.250
He focused on this goal of meditation and
yet could not help but find frustration in

00:09:23.250 --> 00:09:24.250
his efforts.

00:09:24.250 --> 00:09:27.999
It didn’t help that the brothers of the
monastery now openly resented him.

00:09:27.999 --> 00:09:32.560
Steve’s demeanor began to change and become
less optimistic and more obsessed with the

00:09:32.560 --> 00:09:37.910
memory of the repetitive monotony of his old
life before coming to the monastery.

00:09:37.910 --> 00:09:43.889
His tulpa too began to change, no longer fat
with joy, its appearance began to thin.

00:09:43.889 --> 00:09:48.910
What was once an embodiment of laughter and
happiness began to morph into a darker, more

00:09:48.910 --> 00:09:50.869
mischievous entity.

00:09:50.869 --> 00:09:53.279
The pranks too became more dangerous.

00:09:53.279 --> 00:09:57.680
The tulpa began leaving buckets of scalding
hot water above door frames for unsuspecting

00:09:57.680 --> 00:09:58.899
monks to walk through.

00:09:58.899 --> 00:10:02.160
It then began filling the sandals of monks
with snakes.

00:10:02.160 --> 00:10:06.379
Thankfully for the brothers of the monastery,
the snakes weren’t poisonous.

00:10:06.379 --> 00:10:10.579
Until suddenly, on one particular occasion,
they were.

00:10:10.579 --> 00:10:15.889
A pair of Fea’s Vipers appeared in the sandals
of a brother of the monastery, venomous snakes

00:10:15.889 --> 00:10:20.449
that could only be found hundreds of miles
away in the south of Tibet, in a region Steve

00:10:20.449 --> 00:10:23.240
had never heard of and had never been to.

00:10:23.240 --> 00:10:27.890
It was an impossibility for him to have given
birth to the manifestation of this act without

00:10:27.890 --> 00:10:29.709
its requisite knowledge.

00:10:29.709 --> 00:10:34.399
Did this mean the tulpa had gained some means
of self-actualization?

00:10:34.399 --> 00:10:37.970
Could it contemplate its own sentience?

00:10:37.970 --> 00:10:41.869
Seeking to learn more answers about the nature
of the tulpa, Steve studied the teachings

00:10:41.869 --> 00:10:44.879
of the Buddha, and the quest for enlightenment.

00:10:44.879 --> 00:10:48.589
About Nirvana and the end to the cycle of
death and rebirth.

00:10:48.589 --> 00:10:52.679
In his mind, Steve began to intertwine those
ideas with the memory of the mundanity of

00:10:52.679 --> 00:10:58.439
his previous life, and the feelings that lingered
in his stomach of it being unfulfilling and

00:10:58.439 --> 00:10:59.439
empty.

00:10:59.439 --> 00:11:02.889
How he had desperately wanted the daily cycle
of mundanity to end.

00:11:02.889 --> 00:11:04.500
How he had wanted peace.

00:11:04.500 --> 00:11:11.439
Little did he know in doing so he was creating
a manifestation with the express goal of ending

00:11:11.439 --> 00:11:12.509
his life.

00:11:12.509 --> 00:11:17.199
As Steve began to enter longer and deeper
sessions of meditation, the tulpa began to

00:11:17.199 --> 00:11:21.259
grow more self-actualizing and independent
of his will.

00:11:21.259 --> 00:11:24.589
It became harder to control, maleficent.

00:11:24.589 --> 00:11:29.240
And one day, Steve realized he could no longer
picture the laughing buddha that had once

00:11:29.240 --> 00:11:31.040
filled him with joy.

00:11:31.040 --> 00:11:36.579
From that moment on, the tulpa’s face became
unrecognizable, and was no longer in a fixed

00:11:36.579 --> 00:11:41.420
state but in constant movement, so that no
facial features could be visible.

00:11:41.420 --> 00:11:46.110
It was that night the monks had caught the
tulpa holding a knife to Steve’s throat.

00:11:46.110 --> 00:11:50.360
Channeling their meditative power of actualization,
they managed to collectively banish the tulpa

00:11:50.360 --> 00:11:51.769
from the monastery.

00:11:51.769 --> 00:11:53.069
But it was not for long.

00:11:53.069 --> 00:11:58.149
The tulpa began to follow Steve wherever he
went, a physical embodiment of his wish to

00:11:58.149 --> 00:12:01.420
end the repeating cycle of his life and bring
him peace.

00:12:01.420 --> 00:12:05.889
Peace by means of the extinguishing of his
life.

00:12:05.889 --> 00:12:11.259
The existence of SCP-1447-1 was first brought
to the attention of Foundation staff when

00:12:11.259 --> 00:12:17.100
“Steve” arrived at Site 73 seeking sanctuary
from the tulpa he had been running from.

00:12:17.100 --> 00:12:21.399
It is unclear to Foundation staff how the
software mogul came to know of the location

00:12:21.399 --> 00:12:23.079
of site 73.

00:12:23.079 --> 00:12:26.699
All that could be gained from questioning
him on the matter is that he received the

00:12:26.699 --> 00:12:31.679
information from the monks at a lamasery in
Qinghai province, China.

00:12:31.679 --> 00:12:37.910
Steve was given the designation SCP-1447-2
because of his relation to the entity, and

00:12:37.910 --> 00:12:40.649
then placed in secure confinement at the facility.

00:12:40.649 --> 00:12:46.309
Two days later, security personnel made contact
with the entity when it attacked the facility

00:12:46.309 --> 00:12:50.360
in search of the tech mogul, resulting in
the death of two agents.

00:12:50.360 --> 00:12:57.040
The attacks from SCP-1447 ceased when “Steve”
was evacuated via airlift to London, and then

00:12:57.040 --> 00:12:59.170
later moved again to site 60.

00:12:59.170 --> 00:13:04.060
In just three weeks after this change, the
tulpa had already caught up with “Steve”,

00:13:04.060 --> 00:13:09.259
attacking the facility and becoming enraged
by the interference from security personnel,

00:13:09.259 --> 00:13:12.529
slaughtering countless members of SCP staff
in its wake.

00:13:12.529 --> 00:13:16.689
It is here at this facility that the members
of security personnel were first able to use

00:13:16.689 --> 00:13:22.689
high-caliber firepower to push back the tulpa’s
advance into a makeshift concrete enclosure,

00:13:22.689 --> 00:13:27.879
which would eventually come to be SCP-1447-1’s
current containment cell.

00:13:27.879 --> 00:13:33.579
Dr. Rolfus, an SCP researcher, was the first
to interview Steve after assigning him the

00:13:33.579 --> 00:13:34.910
designation SCP-1447-2.

00:13:34.910 --> 00:13:41.759
He was given this designation when Foundation
staff realized that the person known as “Steve”,

00:13:41.759 --> 00:13:47.629
(real name redacted), had in fact never left
the United States for Qinghai Province, and

00:13:47.629 --> 00:13:53.139
had been leading his life as a successful
tech mogul without any notable interruption.

00:13:53.139 --> 00:13:58.170
Researchers became unsure of whether “Steve”
was in fact who he said he was, or instead

00:13:58.170 --> 00:14:02.180
an entity similar to SCP-1447-1.

00:14:02.180 --> 00:14:06.589
When confronted with images of his doppelganger
in news and media reports living out his life

00:14:06.589 --> 00:14:13.059
and assuming his identity, SCP-1447-2 was
unable to explain the anomaly and asserted

00:14:13.059 --> 00:14:18.689
that he was the true original version of himself,
suggesting that a rival technology company,

00:14:18.689 --> 00:14:23.509
or even his own for that matter, may have
hired a look-alike to take his place as head

00:14:23.509 --> 00:14:25.559
of the business in his absence.

00:14:25.559 --> 00:14:31.339
When the public counterpart of SCP-1447-2
recently found deceased, testing of the subject's

00:14:31.339 --> 00:14:35.670
hair and tissue showed no anamalous characteristics
of any kind.

00:14:35.670 --> 00:14:42.009
It is believed SCP-1447-1 may have been somehow
responsible for the mysterious death.

00:14:42.009 --> 00:14:47.970
A prevailing theory regarding the existence
of SCP-1447-2’s counterpart posits that

00:14:47.970 --> 00:14:53.050
Steve may have been in fact able to manifest
two tulpas into existence.

00:14:53.050 --> 00:14:57.910
Steve may have suffered a traumatic mental
breakdown that perhaps, unbeknownst to him,

00:14:57.910 --> 00:15:03.879
led to the creation of a secondary personality
that later manifested itself into existence

00:15:03.879 --> 00:15:07.679
following his training in meditation and practice
in creating a tulpa.

00:15:07.679 --> 00:15:14.649
It may have been this dual manifestation that
led to Steve’s loss of control of SCP-1447-1

00:15:14.649 --> 00:15:16.700
in the first place.

00:15:16.700 --> 00:15:21.889
SCP-1447-2 remains adamant that he has the
power to put an end to the tulpa’s existence

00:15:21.889 --> 00:15:26.939
through the application of methods of concentration
and meditative practice.

00:15:26.939 --> 00:15:34.379
SCP-1447-2 dedicates at the very least 4 hours
a day to meditating on the following topics;

00:15:34.379 --> 00:15:43.079
“SCP-1447-1 is getting weaker, SCP-1447-1
is dying, SCP-1447-1 is unable to maintain

00:15:43.079 --> 00:15:44.329
physical form.”

00:15:44.329 --> 00:15:50.470
To his credit, Foundation researchers have
observed SCP-1447-1’s is severely curtailed

00:15:50.470 --> 00:15:56.079
during periods in which its counterpart engages
in focused meditation on the abolition of

00:15:56.079 --> 00:15:57.220
the tulpa.

00:15:57.220 --> 00:16:04.420
During these periods SCP-1447-1 is almost
completely still, adopting the vajra meditation

00:16:04.420 --> 00:16:05.420
position.

00:16:05.420 --> 00:16:10.639
It is believed that through self-actualization,
the tulpa can meditate on its own existence,

00:16:10.639 --> 00:16:15.199
counteracting the meditative “attacks”
against its ability to exist in its manifested

00:16:15.199 --> 00:16:16.199
form.

00:16:16.199 --> 00:16:19.720
To aid in this endeavor, Foundation staff
have considered different ways to disrupt

00:16:19.720 --> 00:16:21.540
SCP-1447-1’s meditation.

00:16:21.540 --> 00:16:27.709
At first, they suggested a hydrochloric acid
bath be pumped into its enclosure, but then

00:16:27.709 --> 00:16:32.499
withdrew that proposal on fears it would surely
use whatever delivery mechanism into the enclosure

00:16:32.499 --> 00:16:34.389
as a means of escape.

00:16:34.389 --> 00:16:38.310
Further suggestions put forward for the matter
include using microwave emitters to remotely

00:16:38.310 --> 00:16:42.980
heat the interior of the unit, and the use
of high-volume, high-intensity sonic equipment

00:16:42.980 --> 00:16:45.480
proven to inhibit concentration.

00:16:45.480 --> 00:16:49.990
Staff is also instructed to assist in this
effort by channeling positive thoughts incorporating

00:16:49.990 --> 00:16:54.839
the demise and destruction of SCP-1447-1.

00:16:54.839 --> 00:16:58.949
Positive slogans are posted in the hallways
and break rooms around the facility to assist

00:16:58.949 --> 00:17:00.610
in positive thinking.

00:17:00.610 --> 00:17:04.839
Weekly therapy visits for all staff members
are mandatory to ensure an environment of

00:17:04.839 --> 00:17:06.550
strong mental health.

00:17:06.550 --> 00:17:10.870
And complimentary gym memberships are given
out to employees to promote physical wellbeing

00:17:10.870 --> 00:17:12.089
and motivated thinking.

00:17:12.089 --> 00:17:19.189
In the only interview on file with the human
known as SCP-1447-2, “Steve”, Dr. Rolfus

00:17:19.189 --> 00:17:23.760
asked the subject what would happen if the
tulpa were allowed to kill him.

00:17:23.760 --> 00:17:29.389
SCP-1447-2 refused to answer, leaving Foundation
researchers to arrive at two possible theories.

00:17:29.389 --> 00:17:36.820
First, if SCP-1447-1 destroys the human that
is responsible for its existence, then surely

00:17:36.820 --> 00:17:39.429
it too will cease to exist.

00:17:39.429 --> 00:17:43.220
Though when researchers tested this theory
by inflicting different levels of physical

00:17:43.220 --> 00:17:50.610
pain to SCP-1447-2, the tulpa appeared to
have no effect or change in its behavior.

00:17:50.610 --> 00:17:54.990
The second theory, and the one with the greater
support of evidence, is if the tulpa kills

00:17:54.990 --> 00:18:00.889
SCP-1447-2, and it has already demonstrated
that it has the ability to meditate on its

00:18:00.889 --> 00:18:06.740
own existence, then its behavior from then
on out is entirely impossible to predict.

00:18:06.740 --> 00:18:13.690
At the moment, its fixation on SCP-1447-2
has been a large contributing factor to the

00:18:13.690 --> 00:18:15.950
facility’s ability to contain it.

00:18:15.950 --> 00:18:20.620
If it were to decide that its new purpose
was to bring its version of “peace” to

00:18:20.620 --> 00:18:25.320
every life on the planet, there would be little
the Foundation could do to stop it.

00:18:25.320 --> 00:18:31.310
That outcome must be avoided at all costs,
and by extension, the life of the human known

00:18:31.310 --> 00:18:36.409
as SCP-1447-2 must be protected.

00:18:36.409 --> 00:18:42.200
So hopefully, you’ve never had an imaginary
friend manifest itself into existence and

00:18:42.200 --> 00:18:43.830
try to kill you.

00:18:43.830 --> 00:18:48.880
But what we can all agree on is that some
things are better left in our forgotten childhood

00:18:48.880 --> 00:18:49.880
memories.

00:18:49.880 --> 00:18:56.559
Now go check out “SCP-5254 - Gotta Catch
'Em All” and “SCP-6080 - Cartoon Network”

00:18:56.559 --> 00:18:57.420
for more childhood terrors made real!

